      "writtenOn": "2025-01-30T22:54:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now handleDeviceDisconnection is handling only local broadcasts. All stuff to handle external (some of them are for local too) is in connectionStateChanged#STATE_DISCONNECTED so IMHO it is better to have it in one place (better readability and good point to refactor)\n\n*remove Sink Metadata for device if it\u0027s intended disconnection, for not intended check if all devices from \"target group\" are disconnected then remove sink for all of them.*\n- for unintended, we still have to call removeSinkMetadataFromGroupIfWholeUnsynced.\n- for intended, should we remove it? What if we connect it again? As I know for now there is no possibility to disconnect only one device so does not matter.\n- connectionStateChanged is a better place as we have under control order of operation and we not that when we call removeSinkMetadataFromGroupIfWholeUnsynced, the mPausedBroadcastSinks is for sure removed for this device.",
