      "writtenOn": "2025-01-30T22:54:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two types of methods (doubled due to polymorphism) and one helper to avoid code duplication:\n- removeSinkMetadata – Main method to remove sink metadata.\n- removeSinkMetadataFromGroupIfWholeUnsynced – Applies heuristics to clear other sinks from the group.\n- removeSinkMetadataHelper – Equivalent to container removal.\n\nSo not so much.\n\nThe problem is that metadata is used to resume from a device reconnection. We need to keep it, but only if there are other synced sinks. However, if all other sinks become unsynced—regardless of when that happens—we must remove it. This requires adding the check after all removal methods and as a standalone check during device disconnection.",
